        "predicate": "launched",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Component Independence in Projectile Motion",
          "description": "Move to the Ballistics Firing Range. Set the launcher to 45 degrees. The initial velocity vector decomposes into constant horizontal velocity Vx and changing vertical velocity Vy. Gravity acts only vertically (accelerating downward at 9.8 m/s^2), which creates a parabolic path."
        },
